      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Presenting  ‘Coonawarra’, a substantial four-bedroom detached family home combining generous accommodation, period character and a sought-after Killiney address. Part of the rear and the side gardens are not included as there is FPP for 2 detached houses - planning permission under reference D25A/0792.\r\n\r\nBuilt in the 1940s, the property extends to approximately 219 sq. m (2,357 sq. ft), with an additional attic conversion of approximately 23 sq. m (247 sq. ft). Bright, well-proportioned interiors and a choice of reception rooms provide excellent space for both everyday family life and entertaining.\r\n\r\nA welcoming entrance hall leads to the spacious front reception room, where a newly installed stove creates an inviting focal point. A separate dining room connects through double pocket doors to the family room, allowing the rooms to work equally well as individual spaces or together for larger gatherings. The adjoining conservatory enjoys an outlook over the rear garden and provides a peaceful setting in which to relax.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen/breakfast room overlooks the garden and is complemented by a separate pantry and rear porch. A utility room with guest WC completes the ground-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, a generous landing serves four bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with an en suite shower room and walk-in wardrobe. A family bathroom and separate WC are also located on this level. A staircase leads to the converted attic, arranged as three attic rooms, with sea views to Dun Laoghaire and Howth from this elevated position.\r\n\r\nCoonawarra enjoys a convenient setting close to the amenities of Killiney, Dalkey and Glenageary. Local shops, cafés, restaurants and a choice of schools are within easy reach, together with coastal walks and the open spaces of Killiney Hill. DART and bus services provide connections to the city centre and surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nThe house is offered with a reduced garden area, following the separation of two sites within the original grounds. These sites benefit from full planning permission for two houses and are being offered for sale separately. They are not included in the €1,250,000 asking price for Coonawarra.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall — 2.11m x 1.18m\r\nWelcoming entrance with tiled flooring and a rounded window to the side.\r\n\r\nLiving Room — 6.98m x 4.66m\r\nSpacious reception room featuring a stove with marble surround and mahogany mantel. Double pocket doors connect to the family room.\r\n\r\nDining Room — 4.68m x 4.14m\r\nGenerous reception room with a feature open fireplace, marble surround and mahogany mantel. \r\n\r\nFamily Room — 4.68m x 4.22m\r\nComfortable reception room with a gas fireplace, marble surround and mahogany mantel. Double doors open into the conservatory.\r\n\r\nConservatory — 4.77m x 4.00m\r\nBright additional reception space with parquet flooring, windows overlooking the rear garden and doors providing garden access.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Breakfast Room — 2.98m x 4.64m\r\nFitted with bespoke solid wood kitchen units, worktops and tiled splashbacks. Double stainless-steel sink, tiled flooring and space for a breakfast table. Windows overlook the rear garden.\r\n\r\nPantry — 2.68m x 0.88m\r\nUseful additional storage with fitted shelving, tiled flooring and a window links to sunroom.\r\n\r\nUtility Room / Guest WC — 2.00m x 2.44m\r\nWith wash hand basin, under-sink storage and WC. Plumbed for a washing machine.\r\n\r\nRear Porch — 1.35m x 5.01m\r\nTiled flooring and a glazed door to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nFirst-Floor Landing — 5.59m x 5.47m\r\nSpacious, bright landing with access to the hot press and storage press.\r\n\r\nPrincipal Bedroom — 5.29m x 4.39m\r\nGenerous double bedroom to the front with an en suite shower room and a walk-in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nEn Suite Shower Room\r\nWith wash hand basin and shower cubicle, tiled flooring, partially tiled walls and a towel rail.\r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 — 4.11m x 4.82m\r\nDouble bedroom to the front with under-eaves storage and wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 — 4.23m x 3.63m\r\nDouble bedroom to the rear with dual-aspect windows, fitted wardrobes and wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 — 2.00m x 3.97m\r\nBedroom to the rear with triple-aspect windows and wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nBathroom — 1.96m x 2.57m\r\nFitted with a bath, shower screen and wall-mounted shower, wash hand basin and towel rail. Partially tiled walls and cork tiled flooring.\r\n\r\nSeparate WC — 0.95m x 1.65m\r\nWith WC and cork tiled flooring.\r\n\r\nAttic Conversion — 5.67m x 4.07m\r\nAccessed by an open timber staircase and arranged as three attic rooms, two with Velux windows. Sea views from this level of Dun Laoghaire and Howth. Approximately 23 sq. m (247 sq. ft), excluded from the stated main floor area.\r\n\r\nLinks to Sites:   \r\n\r\nSite A:    https://www.myhome.ie/residential/brochure/avalon-avondale-park-killiney-county-dublin/5028734\r\nSite B:    https://www.myhome.ie/residential/brochure/barrow-avondale-park-killiney-county-dublin/5028718"
      },
